    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "9d3807bb-b564-38e5-a898-c8aeccd256d9",
                "word": "slammed",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "58c53b90-cd86-403c-8839-2ebb0700b69c",
                        "entry_id": "9d3807bb-b564-38e5-a898-c8aeccd256d9",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more slammed"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "ac0859dd-b031-4fc9-9793-bc48eb061b5c",
                        "entry_id": "9d3807bb-b564-38e5-a898-c8aeccd256d9",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most slammed"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "010eb1fe-fd64-3c83-91e6-9247fe038f18",
                        "entry_id": "9d3807bb-b564-38e5-a898-c8aeccd256d9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Very busied with work."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e4e20b5-f44a-4e95-886d-f8244e88e743",
                                "sense_id": "010eb1fe-fd64-3c83-91e6-9247fe038f18",
                                "text": "I was just too slammed to intervene. By drink number five he was snapping his fingers to get my attention and his tips were getting smaller and smaller. He was becoming my worst enemy and he could sense it."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "818e06ab-659f-41d1-b45f-7c8410156fa1",
                                "sense_id": "010eb1fe-fd64-3c83-91e6-9247fe038f18",
                                "text": "Or, worse yet, you've been so slammed with working on a massive science project about helium that you haven't stayed caught up in any of your other classes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ec2ac74-a96e-4e32-bdc4-ff5bf1eb7ef1",
                                "sense_id": "010eb1fe-fd64-3c83-91e6-9247fe038f18",
                                "text": "It's because you are fabulous, of course, but also because if they are so slammed that they can't even make time for a face-to-face interview, trust me, they want to check the box that this position is filled […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2ed1e05d-c4b3-4b62-929c-dc17491d940a",
                                "sense_id": "010eb1fe-fd64-3c83-91e6-9247fe038f18",
                                "text": "She justifies the systemic response by constructing demand and positioning herself as 'absolutely slammed' in a 'work load intensive environment.' Una acknowledges consumer disappointment: 'you know that's not what they are there for'[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "69011275-e84b-474a-ba69-99669889c8f9",
                                "sense_id": "010eb1fe-fd64-3c83-91e6-9247fe038f18",
                                "text": "“We've been jammed with so much, trying to get our TV show back on the air,” Buck apologized. “I've just been so slammed with so many things.” I said it was no problem. The sun streaked past my passenger window."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5a42fafe-f1b0-47e6-903b-75fac8f0eb8d",
                                "sense_id": "010eb1fe-fd64-3c83-91e6-9247fe038f18",
                                "text": "“I have several clients, and with a buyer's market, I'm very slammed.” “That's okay. I understand.” “Well, I was going to suggest something. Seeing how I am showing houses all over, when in the area and free, I can stop by[…]”"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "52c76f92-30d5-33ea-afce-f66da6b1d7aa",
                        "entry_id": "9d3807bb-b564-38e5-a898-c8aeccd256d9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Drunk."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "095072e6-2825-44bf-aba6-91739f83629e",
                                "sense_id": "52c76f92-30d5-33ea-afce-f66da6b1d7aa",
                                "text": "Q. You get very slammed? A. Yes. But if I just go out for social drinks, a couple of pints. A. And how often do you go out and get really slammed? Q. About once a fortnight. But I get stoned [i.e. on cannabis] all the time. It's better."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dfcaabce-6c7e-408d-959d-d75c8b8c81ea",
                                "sense_id": "52c76f92-30d5-33ea-afce-f66da6b1d7aa",
                                "text": "By the time it was my turn, I was more slammed than I had been in a very long time, maybe ever. Especially around that many people. My eyelids felt heavy. […] And everybody as drunk as me. They wouldn't even remember."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "89d5affb-9446-4c48-8748-78aca4d43771",
                                "sense_id": "52c76f92-30d5-33ea-afce-f66da6b1d7aa",
                                "text": "I expected them to get absolutely slammed, especially with all the free booze on offer, but they drank moderately and spent most of the time talking or dancing. They didn't interact with the other patrons,[…]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0bf1f1db-89f3-3c18-8d71-511c7d197662",
                        "entry_id": "9d3807bb-b564-38e5-a898-c8aeccd256d9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Packed, crowded, (of a venue) full of would-be customers."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "97614a6e-d2d6-43bf-9ae8-3cf52f435262",
                                "sense_id": "0bf1f1db-89f3-3c18-8d71-511c7d197662",
                                "text": "Lauren was at work the next morning, absolutely slammed, the waiting area filled with people and a crowd outside all waiting to get in because it was Father's Day and everyone wanted to treat their dad. Their wait time was[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9c84e683-068f-4959-b738-86fee57d32cc",
                                "sense_id": "0bf1f1db-89f3-3c18-8d71-511c7d197662",
                                "text": "Then, one evening in the spring of 2002, the bar was absolutely slammed. It was a Tuesday, ten-cent-hot-wings night, and the local Pagan's Saints gang had the 19th Hole overflowing with leathers, mullets, and ponytails."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a2f92e9f-8837-4557-9fd3-0bde49cde869",
                                "sense_id": "0bf1f1db-89f3-3c18-8d71-511c7d197662",
                                "text": "My flight landed in Vegas at around five. Not surprisingly the Las Vegas airport was even more slammed than Denver's."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c8d542fd-9923-48c3-9922-f83a650e5fcc",
                                "sense_id": "0bf1f1db-89f3-3c18-8d71-511c7d197662",
                                "text": "The tavern was absolutely slammed, but we finally found a crease at the bar where we could sidle up to and order a pint. The redhaired Irish lass tending bar poured us a nice glass of stout and we began to check out the clientele."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "62d44d00-f87a-4e1b-a9a9-644aa43cd3b0",
                                "sense_id": "0bf1f1db-89f3-3c18-8d71-511c7d197662",
                                "text": "It was a Sunday and we'd been absolutely slammed. I think there was some kind of concert in the town-centre and the footfall absolutely killed us. I hadn't planned for it at all. I'd sent the staff home early when everything turned[…]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
